{"The event listener gates all cleanup logic (role removal, client removal, group removal) behind ADMIN_FINE_GRAINED_AUTHZ (V1 only), so when V2 is enabled, role and group removal events are silently ignored even though MgmtPermissionsV2 inherits working roles() and groups() from MgmtPermissions": 0.7648082375526428, "ClientPermissionsV2 queries resources using ownerId=server.getId(), but AdminPermissionsSchema creates resources owned by resourceServer.getClientId(); this prevents finding the intended resources and makes permission checks incorrectly deny access": 0.31799665093421936, "getClientsWithPermission incorrectly includes the global 'Clients' resource name in the returned set of client IDs, causing NullPointerException when downstream components like AvailableRoleMappingResource attempt to look up this client via realm.getClientById(cid)": 0.8001284003257751, "In ClientPermissionsV2.hasPermission(ClientModel, String), when no per-client resource exists, getResourceTypeResource() is called but can return null, and the null value is then passed to findByResource(server, resource) which requires a non-null resource, causing a NullPointerException": 0.908464252948761, "The getEvaluationContext method is defined but completely unused within ClientPermissionsV2 since the only method that previously utilized it (canExchangeTo) was overridden to throw an UnsupportedOperationException": 0.5749449133872986}